5:03:25.000-05:00","title":"What are you doing this week?","url":"","score":13,"flags":0,"comment_count":20,"description":"\u003cp\u003eWhat are you doing this week? Feel free to share!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKeep in mind it’s OK to do nothing at all, too.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"What are you doing this week? Feel free to share!\r\n\r\nKeep in mind it’s OK to do nothing at all, too.","submitter_user":"caius","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ask","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/dsklys","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/dsklys/what_are_you_doing_this_week"},{"short_id":"tcfgqw","created_at":"2019-08-12T04:22:03.000-05:00","title":"Persistent document caching/mirroring recommendations","url":"","score":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":4,"description":"\u003cp\u003eI'm looking for a way to archive some images and PDFs for a search-engine-like application I'm building. Concretely, I'd like some sort of hybrid HTTP cache / document store, that ideally:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ecaches URLs persistently and indefinitely\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esupports some form of versioned updates, i.e., refresh the source document but keep the original around if it has changed\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI'm prepared to roll my own, but it feels like this problem might have been solved in a reusable way before. Any pointers?\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"I'm looking for a way to archive some images and PDFs for a search-engine-like application I'm building. Concretely, I'd like some sort of hybrid HTTP cache / document store, that ideally:\r\n\r\n1. caches URLs persistently and indefinitely\r\n2. supports some form of versioned updates, i.e., refresh the source document but keep the original around if it has changed\r\n\r\nI'm prepared to roll my own, but it feels like this problem might have been solved in a reusable way before. Any pointers?","submitter_user":"inactive-user","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ask","web"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/tcfgqw","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/tcfgqw/persistent_document_caching_mirroring"},{"short_id":"qairy5","created_at":"2019-08-12T04:13:27.000-05:00","title":"Austin: Python frame stack sampler for CPython","url":"https://github.com/P403n1x87/austin","score":8,"flags":0,"comment_count":6,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"gthm","user_is_author":false,"tags":["performance","python"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/qairy5","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/qairy5/austin_python_frame_stack_sampler_for"},{"short_id":"d6gxqv","created_at":"2019-08-12T04:07:23.000-05:00","title":"Resurrecting simnet","url":"https://zinascii.com/2019/resurrecting-simnet.html","score":6,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"wiedi","user_is_author":false,"tags":["illumos","networking","testing","unix"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/d6gxqv","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/d6gxqv/resurrecting_simnet"},{"short_id":"m8um3n","created_at":"2019-08-12T02:13:50.000-05:00","title":"Xfce 4.14 released","url":"https://xfce.org/about/news/?post=1565568000","score":33,"flags":0,"comment_count":16,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"klingtnet","user_is_author":false,"tags":["linux","release"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/m8um3n","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/m8um3n/xfce_4_14_released"},{"short_id":"2le8qi","created_at":"2019-08-11T21:59:19.000-05:00","title":"Postgres 12 highlight - SQL/JSON path","url":"https://paquier.xyz/postgresql-2/postgres-12-jsonpath/","score":18,"flags":0,"comment_count":2,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"friendlysock","user_is_author":false,"tags":["api","databases"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/2le8qi","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/2le8qi/postgres_12_highlight_sql_json_path"},{"short_id":"nf8klf","created_at":"2019-08-11T21:46:29.000-05:00","title":"Power stuff an